thank you very much distinguished guests  from europe and beyond dear colleagues  and friends  welcome welcome to this very special  edition of the brussels economic forum  it is a special edition because for the  first time  all keynote speakers of this forum are  women  let me thank angela merkel jacinda  aldern  christine lagarde and all the speakers  for joining us today  and it's a special edition also because  europe's economy is  finally back on track and allow me to  start with a few numbers  in our spring economic forecast we  projected  our economy to grow by 4.2  this year and by 4.4 percent  in 2022 and the numbers  are looking better and better as we go  through the year  this means that in 18 months from now  all 27 member states  will be back on track recovered from the  crisis  no one expected this just a few months  ago  but it is not by chance this  is the result of the policy decisions we  took since the very early days of the  pandemic  and they have paid off and i would like  to mention two of them  the first is our work on vaccines  vaccination is now allowing our  countries and our economies to reopen  and the second factor is the  unprecedented  economic stimulus measures that we have  put together  at the european level and at the  national level  so to my first point our work on  vaccination  today more than sixty percent of  european adults have received  at least one shot and 41  are fully vaccinated and this is good  but we all know that we are not out of  the woods yet  we also have to support our neighbors  and we have to support the rest of the  world  because we will only be able to turn  this page  when we have reached immunity worldwide  now on my second point the economic  outlook  we have learned our lessons of the great  financial crisis of 2008.  so in the early days of this crisis  we immediately enabled member states to  take action  through the general escape clause for  example or through the temporary state  aid framework  and the full flexibilization of the eu  budget  and in parallel we worked on the first  european initiative  to finance short time work we called it  sure sure supported almost 30  million workers in europe last year  saving jobs and companies  and all that was about repairing now for  the long term the recovery  we also started working one year ago on  next generation eu  our package of 800 billion euro  in today's prices is the biggest  recovery package in europe since the  marshall plan  two weeks ago the commission issued  bonds to finance next generation eu  it was a big success seven times  oversubscribed  and with that we are ready to start  disbursing the pre-financing  in other words the funds will start  flowing to member states and  into our economy already in july  it's a first it's unprecedented  and it is precisely what europe needs  right now  because with next generation eu we are  reshaping our continent for decades  ahead  we're digitizing our economies as we've  never done before  and we are making the european green  deal a reality  we are equipping our societies to be  stronger  and to be more resilient  the impact of these investments will be  very tangible  next generation eu alone will boost our  economy  by 2 of gdp  but numbers only tell part of the story  the 800 billion euros from next  generation eu  are there to serve a purpose a vision of  the continent we want to build  we're not just bouncing back to  pre-crisis level  but we are bouncing forward into the  future  and in the last two weeks i have started  visiting our member states  and i have already seen what change next  generation  you can bring to our economies for  example in greece  next generation you will create 5g  corridors  and invest in high-speed broadband  infrastructure  to connect the whole country  or in denmark i visited an electrolyzer  that will use power from from windmills  and  biomass to produce clean hydrogen  and the project will receive funding  from next generation eu  and it will start producing clean  hydrogen by the end of the year  and it will fuel zero emission transport  in the copenhagen area or for example in  luxembourg  i met quantum experts who are working on  a new technology  for safe communications via satellite  and this will protect  our data flows from cyber attacks  and it is a project that can help create  jobs different jobs in many other eu  countries  and strengthen europe's tech sovereignty  these examples and many many more show  with next generation eu we are doing  more  than just increase our gdp  we are building a new economy digital  circular and sustainable  so this is just the beginning we have a  long  exciting road ahead of us next  generation you is  the recovery europe reads now and for  the future  so let's make it a success let's do that  together  and again thank you very much and again  welcome to the brussels economic forum
 

